# Conformance probe pack for absent-value sentinels (spec 0.9) in a sequential
# `bits` layout, most-significant-bit-first. Public. No kinds. Exercises
# ruling 4: a sentinel written for an absent key is not content for a
# presence bit, an `opt` bit or a chain's `fx` bit, so a block that would
# write only sentinels is left out and its bit is 0; an item of a `while`
# group whose every field holds a sentinel is still an item (ruling 5); a
# sentinel compared after `swap`; and a field without `absent` that writes
# zero bits as before.
#
#   x 8 | p.1 p.2, 6 zero bits | p.1: y 8, z 8 | p.2: w 8 |
#   7 zero bits, opt bit | opt: n 16 (little-endian) |
#   chain: c1 7, fx, c2 7, fx | val 8 |
#   recs while: 1, label 16 (ASCII), qty 8 ... 0 | zero bits to the byte
format     conformance-absent-seq
version    0.9.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field   probe.x  8  uint  absent 255
presence p 2
pad 6
if p.1
  field  probe.y  8  uint  absent 0
  field  probe.z  8  uint  absent 255
end
if p.2
  field  probe.w  8  uint
end
pad 7
opt
  field  probe.n  16  uint  swap  absent 65280
end
chain
  field  probe.c1  7  uint  absent 127
  fx
  field  probe.c2  7  uint  absent 0
  fx
end
field   probe.val  8  uint
group   probe.recs while
  field  probe.label  16  ascii  absent 0
  field  probe.qty    8   uint   absent 255
end
